// Swing feel-equation beside the metronome mark: "♩ = 120  ♫ = ♩ ♪" with the
// quarter + eighth under a triplet "3" bracket (LilyPond's own swing idiom,
// \rhythm { 8[ 8] } = \rhythm { \tuplet 3/2 { 4 8 } }). The equation is drawn to the RIGHT of "= 120", so its ink reaches
// far past a plain metronome mark and sits over the first beamed group. The
// outside-staff stacker must see that full left-anchored width (swing included)
// and lift the whole mark clear of the beam AND the fermata that rise under it —
// otherwise the swing symbol prints straight on the beam/fermata.
title "Tempo Swing"
composer "Lily#"

part m { clef treble }

section A {
  m { tempo 120 swing
      g''8 a, a@fermata a d e f g | }
}

form main { A }

score main "tempo-swing" {
  staff m
}
